C EXAMPLE - INTEGER LOOPS AND CONDITIONS

PURPOSE: Use variables, while, if/else, and write().
Write /tmp/count.c via MCP write_file:

  int main() {
      int n = 0;
      while (n < 3) {
          if (n == 1) {
              write(1, "B", 1);
          } else {
              write(1, "A", 1);
          }
          n = n + 1;
      }
      write(1, "\n", 1);
      return 0;
  }

Run separately:
  cc /tmp/count.c
  as /tmp/count.s
  /tmp/a.out
Expected stdout: ABA and newline.

The C subset supports while and if/else but not for.
Prefix/postfix ++ and -- are supported for local int variables only.
Comparisons belong to conditions; avoid boolean operators and casts.
If cc accepts the file but as rejects output, inspect the generated
assembly and simplify the program or branches (source/output limits).
